      ":question/problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=\u27e8{e}^{x+y},\\,{e}^{x+y}\u27e9$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,\\operatorname{ln}\u20612)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $F$ is conservative.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1),$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$"
